WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.375
Let’s walk through Communications.

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:06.675
Use communications for deliberate coordination with a known audience

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:06.825
.

00:00:06.825 --> 00:00:10.088
Verify the recipient and purpose before sending, and keep

00:00:10.088 --> 00:00:13.812
rulings or requests that require durable workflow history in their

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:16.688
owning artifact or RFI surface.

00:00:16.688 --> 00:00:20.087
On this slide, send direct operational text to White

00:00:20.087 --> 00:00:24.125
Cell and review the isolated inbound and outbound history

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:24.288
.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.835
In practice, keep consequential rulings in the RFI workflow

00:00:28.835 --> 00:00:28.998
;

00:00:28.998 --> 00:00:33.060
use communications for coordination and explicit messages

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:33.160
.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.285
When you are ready, use Open Communications to move

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:37.972
to the live surface.

00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:40.810
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:40.960
.
